The dataset used originates from the Kaggle (Credit Card Fraud Detection, 2018), which is named as Credit Card Fraud Detection dataset, comprising 284,807 transactions made by European cardholders 
in September 2013. The dataset exhibiting a profound class imbalance with 284,315 legitimate cases (99.83%) and only 492 fraudulent ones (0.17%). It includes 31 attributes, 28 unlabeled features are 
undisclosed using Principal Component Analysis (PCA) for confidentiality (Kasasbeh et al., 2022b), and 3 labeled features (Time, Amount, Class). The target variable, Class, is a binary indicator where 0 
signifying a valid transaction and 1 signifying a fraudulent one.
Dataset Link: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/mlg-ulb/creditcardfraud
